{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788328050935702001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"mechanical-bitter-basenji","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"2cc3118877ebbc53fd78a33c9842222cd6914bbdc6fe34c142f003ffcf0a89b5","event_uuid":"73bb06c8-6083-4784-a478-07063f8f4900","position":{"commit_sha":"2a3805fdf380a805451fa3fad1bb0a6db5b3c7b2","position":"1788314329437517001-73bb06c8-6083-4784-a478-07063f8f4900"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8b6e2d2484e0bcede6ba66db381304883d2a0e0d36ec7bdd338fe4e0a91dfb15","event_uuid":"419256cb-0208-4946-b49c-6a7c05a7d04d","position":{"commit_sha":"805fec26bdd2ce3c88bc96098652fd84ad38a7c3","position":"1788314341271982001-419256cb-0208-4946-b49c-6a7c05a7d04d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f1c7035a832d89298e3c182eeae032f98de5a7ff312ccc1943b75a1f953699fb","event_uuid":"f9fd1e1e-3e8c-46a0-b747-33aa9371c388","position":{"commit_sha":"7ab66472bfc470656bade258b901bcab29b160f3","position":"1788315186412804001-f9fd1e1e-3e8c-46a0-b747-33aa9371c388"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788314329437517001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f9fd1e1e-3e8c-46a0-b747-33aa9371c388","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"f1a4-1b43-b720-4dab"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe legacy `reconcile` family spans CLI registration, direct-engine modes, library/MCP `mode=` acceptance, compatibility profiles, exit behavior, manifests/tallies, and `bridge_state/reconcile-check.json`. It is not a simple rename. In particular, historical `\"reconcile-check\"` state appears in `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py:658,717`.\n\n## Approach\n\nThis container separates canonical bridge capability migration from deletion of legacy command/mode/state surfaces. Child 1 maps and implements all useful reconcile-check observables under `bridge preview`, `bridge fsck`, `bridge status`, or one coherent new bridge diagnostic subverb. Child 2 removes CLI/direct-engine modes and persisted-state compatibility only after migration. Child 3 removes library/MCP compatibility methods and schemas after the new bridge contracts are live.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Canonical bridge operations retain or explicitly retire every current reconcile-check observable with documented evidence.\n- [ ] No live route, mode, state path, docs, schema, or compatibility profile retains `reconcile` or `reconcile-check` vocabulary.\n- [ ] Persisted historical reconcile-check data is migrated or read by a narrowly retained decoder until safe to retire.\n- [ ] CLI, Python, and MCP consumers use explicit bridge operations rather than compatibility `mode=` dispatch.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"none","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","f1a4-1b43-b720-4dab"],["parent","78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"Why no repository files change on this container: the three child migrations own implementation, documentation, and schema edits. Where evidence lives: the child Gerrit changes and their completion-verifier records establish each substantive outcome.","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["janitor","reconciler","breaking-change","compatibility"],"ticket_id":"0cfc-e511-8f8a-4c8b","ticket_type":"story","title":"Retire the reconcile and reconcile-check compatibility family","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["73bb06c8-6083-4784-a478-07063f8f4900","419256cb-0208-4946-b49c-6a7c05a7d04d","f9fd1e1e-3e8c-46a0-b747-33aa9371c388"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788328050935702001,"uuid":"a12e2d1c-f72f-4af2-8796-df4d490e718e"}